From: chenshuailin <chen.shuailin@intellif.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 17:34:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] port: idle-LoRA prep on bs==0 idle (dp-attn
 gathered-MoE crash)

Root cause of the flaky CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS in the DSPARK full-loop RL
smokes (dspark_full_loop_smoke13/14/15): an IDLE-mode eager forward on a
dp-attention rank crashes in the MoE dp-sync path shortly after a LoRA adapter
swap on rollout resume.

Mechanism (GPU-repro'd + instrumented on node53):
- A dp-attention rank with no local requests runs an eager IDLE forward with
  batch_size == 0 (0 local tokens). _execute_idle gated the eager LoRA batch_info
  refresh on `batch_size > 0`, so bs==0 idle skipped it and kept the PREVIOUS
  forward's batch_info (observed: preexisting bi.bs=1/num_seg=1/max_len=6).
- Under dp-attention the MoE FFN runs on the GATHERED global buffer, so the idle
  rank still executes the shared-expert LoRA on gathered_rows > 0 (observed
  gathered_rows=6, local_input_rows=0). The layer-level `input_.shape[0] > 0`
  guard in lora/layers.py cannot skip it: it sees the gathered rows, not the
  local 0.
- The LoRA shrink kernel grids over batch_info.bs / seg_indptr (stale). When a
  prior larger forward left a big segment layout and the current gathered idle
  buffer is small (varied batch sizes on rollout resume + adapter-swap pool
  churn), the kernel over-reads the buffer -> illegal address. It surfaces as a
  sticky async fault at the next synchronizing op (dp-gather all_reduce or an
  FP8/FP4 MoE GEMM), which is why the reported frame varies across smokes.

Fix: run the eager idle LoRA prep on EVERY idle eager forward, including
batch_size == 0. Preparing with all-None ids on bs==0 yields an EMPTY consistent
batch_info (num_segments==0) so the LoRA kernels launch 0 programs (safe no-op)
instead of reading stale state. Mirrors the decode cuda-graph runner's idle-LoRA
refresh. use_cuda_graph=False keeps it on the eager batch_info (IDLE is a
cuda-graph MODE, so forward-construction prep targets the static graph buffers).

Validation (node53 csl_dspark_r1, production DSPARK+FP4+dp8 config, graphs ON):
pre-fix a large-burst->tiny-idle shape-thrash repro crashed on the first swap
step with the exact smoke path (_execute_idle -> _run_moe_ffn_dp_sync -> illegal
memory access); post-fix the same driver ran 12+ (ongoing, 0 scheduler exceptions) swap steps clean.

